# Fuel-web user guide (required with every feature)

Whenever you finish a **user-facing feature** (new screen, major workflow, or DoD for Features 1–18), update:

`apps/fuel-web/doc/HOW_TO_USE.md`

## What to add

1. A clear numbered section title matching the feature (e.g. “## 8. Online payments”).
2. **How to use** — click-by-click steps a new pump staff member can follow.
3. **How it works** — one short paragraph on what the feature does in the business (e.g. Concept A vs B).
4. Update the **Typical daily flow** checklist if the feature changes the daily sequence.
5. Do **not** put developer/API details in HOW_TO_USE — keep that in FEATURE_WISE_SUMMARY / code comments.

## When finishing a feature

After Definition of Done summary, confirm HOW_TO_USE was updated before asking the user to confirm and move to the next feature.

## Shared UI reminder

Date / time inputs in fuel-web must use `DatePicker` from `@companyio/platform-ui` (`enableTime` when needed). Never use native `type="date"` or `type="datetime-local"` in fuel-web features.
